Historical Defect Dataset

 Purpose

This directory is used for the historical defect knowledge base of the Intelligent Bug Diagnosis Platform.

The knowledge base will contain historical bug reports collected from publicly available Mozilla, Apache, and Eclipse bug datasets.

 Dataset Sources

The planned historical defect datasets are:

- Mozilla bug reports
- Apache bug reports
- Eclipse bug reports

These datasets are used to identify patterns in previously reported software defects and support semantic retrieval of similar historical bugs.

 Data Processing

The historical defect data will be processed through the following stages:

1. Dataset collection
2. Data cleaning
3. Data standardization
4. Bug report field extraction
5. Text chunking
6. Embedding generation
7. Vector database indexing
8. Semantic similarity search

Bug Report Information

Relevant information may include:

- Bug ID
- Bug title
- Bug description
- Stack trace
- Error information
- Comments
- Affected component
- Resolution
- Status
- Source repository

Privacy and Licensing

Only publicly available datasets will be used.

Dataset licensing and usage conditions will be reviewed before incorporating datasets into the project.
